['THE ATTENDANCE SHEET','A woman called me Employee Forty-Seven. Dad said she had made a mistake. He crossed out my name and wrote his instead.'],
['PERSONNEL CONTINUITY','They asked him to come into the meeting room. “Keep singing,” he told me. “Then I’ll always know where you are.”'],
['BEHIND THE DOOR','I heard a chair scrape. Then something scraped above me. Dad said, “I accept the transfer. Let him leave.” The door never opened.'],
['THE FIRST FOOTPRINT','The ceiling moved. A hand I almost recognized reached between the tiles. I stopped singing because I wanted to ask if it was him.'],
['THE SONG','When I cried, the footsteps hurried. When I sang, they rested. I kept singing. I thought he was still trying to find the stairs.'],
['THE NEXT VISITOR','You followed me like you knew the way home. I asked you where Dad was. The office heard you take his place. Now I have to wait again.']
